ata-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Sensor</th><th>fx, fy, cx, cy px</th><th>Lever mm</th><th>log(R) rad</th><th>td ms</th><th>Readout ms</th><th>t_ga ms</th><th>Reprojection px</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>cam0</th><td>334.1, 334.1, 272.0, 318.5</td><td>[−12.5, +38.4, +17.3]</td><td>[+0.0109, +0.0025, −1.5656]</td><td>+1.24</td><td>global</td><td></td><td>0.161</td></tr><tr><th>cam1</th><td>334.0, 333.9, 269.6, 318.4</td><td>[−12.2, −60.8, +16.7]</td><td>[+0.0080, +0.0023, −1.5642]</td><td>+1.25</td><td>global</td><td></td><td>0.167</td></tr><tr><th>cam2</th><td>775.1, 775.2, 960.1, 535.7</td><td>[−12.5, −11.2, +16.1]</td><td>[+0.0066, +0.0108, −3.1361]</td><td>−5.84</td><td>32.36</td><td></td><td>0.449</td></tr><tr><th>IMU (base)</th><td></td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td></td><td>−5.08 ± 0.04</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Lever arms and rotations are each sensor in the base IMU frame; rotation is log(R) in rad. td is the time offset to the base IMU, t_imu = t_sensor + td. Reprojection is the median per camera (all cameras: median 0.175 px): how well the model fits the corners, not how accurate it is.</p>", "check": "<div class=ex-callout><p><b>No published reference.</b> No published calibration exists for this device, so this page has nothing to compare against. What we can show is how much each value moves over the 10 hand-held recordings. <a href=\"/benchmark/results/looper-insight9/\">All 10 recordings and tools: Dataset eval →</a></p></div>", "config": "<p>The marked lines are the choices that matter for this rig:</p><ul class=list><li><code>camera_input.free_intrinsics</code>: Camera intrinsics stay free in the camera + IMU solve.</li><li><code>camera_input.cameras</code>: The colour camera (cam2) has a rolling shutter, so its readout time is estimated.</li><li><code>solve.estimate_t_ga</code>: Estimates t_ga, the time offset between the gyroscope and the accelerometer.</li><li><code>solve.sigma_g</code>: IMU noise from a still recording of this unit, measured density × 2.5. The other three sigmas are set the same way.</li></ul><p class=note>This is the config of the run on this page, with every path cut to its file name. Point the paths at your copy.</p><p>The solve took about 6 min on one desktop. It writes <code>cam_imu.json</code>, a calibration YAML and a report beside the config.</p><dl class=ex-kv><dt>MVIS</dt><dd>MVIS main, measured-noise batch of 2026-11-08</dd><dt>Run date</dt><dd>2026-11-08</dd><dt>Data</dt><dd><a href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/calibench-vi/datasets/tree/main/looper-insight9\">Calibench, looper-insight9/ →</a></dd><dt>Config</dt><dd><code>looper_insight9_bag1_cam_imu.yaml</code>, above</dd><dt>Command</dt><dd><code>mvis cam-imu -c looper_insight9_bag1_cam_imu.yaml</code></dd></dl>", "dataset": "<div class=two><div><ul class=list><li>Hand-held recording 1 of 10, about 66 s. The run uses the whole recording.</li><li>Cameras: two 544 × 640 global-shutter mono cameras at 20 Hz and a 1920 × 1088 rolling-shutter colour camera at about 4.3 Hz, all fitted with the equidistant lens model. IMU at 400 Hz.</li><li>Board: AprilGrid 6×6, tag 55 mm, spacing 0.3, t36h11.</li><li>Access is by automatic approval on the Hub; the data is CC BY-NC 4.0, commercial use by request.</li><li>Solve window: 66.4 s.</li></ul><p>Download: <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/calibench-vi/datasets/tree/main/looper-insight9\">Calibench, looper-insight9/ →</a> The recordings are listed there, not copied here.</p></div><div><figure class=board><svg viewBox=\"-33.0 -33.0 478.5 478.5\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"AprilGrid 6 by 6, to scale\"><rect x=\"-33.0\" y=\"-33.0\" width=\"478.5\" height=\"478.5\" fill=\"#fff\"/>